# 2. CASH ON DELIVERY — CORRECT PAYMENT LIFECYCLE

Cash on Delivery must NEVER be marked as completed or collected before the order is actually delivered.

Implement separate order and payment states.

For COD:

- Order placed: Payment status = Pending.
- Order confirmed: Payment status = Pending.
- Food preparing: Payment status = Pending.
- Out for Delivery: Payment status = Pending.
- Delivered: Payment status can become Paid/Collected only when delivery confirmation and cash collection are confirmed.

Do not automatically mark COD as paid just because an order was created or dispatched.

Add a proper delivery confirmation and cash collection action for the delivery partner.

If the delivery partner confirms delivery but cash collection is not confirmed, preserve the appropriate outstanding payment state and make this visible to the admin.

Ensure order status and payment status are not treated as the same field.

The customer, admin and delivery partner must see consistent payment information.

